From: BL6000 Pro Ubuntu Touch port
Subject: [PATCH] (halium) libaudioclient: don't wait for AudioFlinger for audio session ids

Halium 11 runs without AudioFlinger ("get rid of using AudioFlinger for
recording"): recording audio comes from /dev/socket/micshm through
CameraRecordService. AudioSystem::acquireAudioSessionId() and
releaseAudioSessionId() still call get_audio_flinger(), which loops forever
("AudioFlinger not published, waiting...") when the service does not exist.
~AudioRecord() calls releaseAudioSessionId(), so stopping a camera video
recording hangs camera_service: MPEG4Writer never writes the moov atom and
the app freezes.

AudioSource::dataCallback() also calls AudioRecord::getInputFramesLost()
-> AudioSystem::getInputFramesLost() -> get_audio_flinger() *while holding
AudioSource::mLock*; stop() then deadlocks in AudioSource::setStopTimeUs()
(native stack captured with debuggerd on the BL6000 Pro, camera_service is
32-bit).

Treat the session-id calls as no-ops and report 0 lost input frames when
media.audio_flinger is not registered.

---
 media/libaudioclient/AudioSystem.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/media/libaudioclient/AudioSystem.cpp
+++ b/media/libaudioclient/AudioSystem.cpp
@@ uint32_t AudioSystem::getInputFramesLost(audio_io_handle_t ioHandle)
 {
+    // Halium: no AudioFlinger (mic data comes from micshm); nothing is lost here.
+    if (defaultServiceManager()->checkService(String16("media.audio_flinger")) == 0)
+        return 0;
     const sp<IAudioFlinger>& af = AudioSystem::get_audio_flinger();
@@ void AudioSystem::acquireAudioSessionId(audio_session_t audioSession, pid_t pid, uid_t uid)
 {
+    // Halium: there is no AudioFlinger; never block waiting for it here.
+    if (defaultServiceManager()->checkService(String16("media.audio_flinger")) == 0)
+        return;
     const sp<IAudioFlinger>& af = AudioSystem::get_audio_flinger();
     if (af != 0) {
         af->acquireAudioSessionId(audioSession, pid, uid);
@@ void AudioSystem::releaseAudioSessionId(audio_session_t audioSession, pid_t pid)
 {
+    // Halium: there is no AudioFlinger; never block waiting for it here.
+    if (defaultServiceManager()->checkService(String16("media.audio_flinger")) == 0)
+        return;
     const sp<IAudioFlinger>& af = AudioSystem::get_audio_flinger();
     if (af != 0) {
         af->releaseAudioSessionId(audioSession, pid);
